## The red this change carries and does not cause

`driver#anOwnedFunctionIsInItsOwnersFile` is red on the base commit `ae2373cb` itself, and this change is not why.
`git show ae2373cb:tools/loop/layout.tsv | grep -c 'action_add\|cmd_publish_refused'` prints `0`, and so does the same
read of `adb79f6f`'s — the base's own `layout.tsv` owns neither function. The diff touches none of that case's inputs
(`git diff --cached HEAD --stat -- tools/loop/layout.tsv tools/loop/report.sh tools/loop/state.sh` is empty: the only
`tools/loop/` file it edits is `run.sh`, whose rows the case does not read for this assertion), so the case that reads
`layout_owned_refusals` over the engine reports the same two rows on the base as here:

    report.sh defines action_add and its row does not own it
    state.sh defines cmd_publish_refused and its row does not own it

The first of the two is the row this landing records as carried; the second stands beside it on the same base. Carried,
not caused here.

