## The archive

$ openspec archive fix-a-continuation-is-handed-what-its-first-read --yes --skip-specs
Proposal warnings in proposal.md (non-blocking):
  ⚠ Why section should not exceed 1000 characters
Task status: ✓ Complete
Skipping spec updates (--skip-specs flag provided).
Change 'fix-a-continuation-is-handed-what-its-first-read' archived as '2026-11-25-fix-a-continuation-is-handed-what-its-first-read'.
exit 0

The warning is the CLI's length preference for the `Why` section, not an artifact defect: `--strict` validated the
change, and the reason this section is long is the correction the implementation established — the per-child repeat
rule cannot answer a continuation, and the ledger rule can — which is the sentence a reader of this record needs.
`openspec archive` did not touch the shipped spec (`--skip-specs`): `git diff openspec/specs/` is empty afterwards, and
the only staged change there is the cherry-pick's own.
